# Local Chitchat backport preparation

Following the retained feasibility refusal, prepare local source patches only.
No root dependency adoption, registry publication, installation or server use.
The exact Chitchat 0.11.1 archive and old refusals remain immutable.

Keep four successive inputs distinct: B (original), M (block-metadata bound
only), L (M plus the two explicit lifetime annotations only), Z (L plus Zstd
0.14.3 only). Record the baseline before each change. Never combine these into
one unreviewed hypothesis or change an original threshold/assertion.

The new minimal bound contract is a positive threshold of one and a one-byte
string. The observer records the original 37-case payload/threshold matrix and
all bounds as data, including baseline failures; its successful process exit is
not a passing bound contract. Candidate contracts independently assert bounds.
The original broad snapshot and its seven malformed/context controls stay exact
and must actually pass on the final Z input before any combined acceptance.

The DeltaSerializer observation uses only supported mtu>=100, a fixed node/key,
seeded ASCII values and lengths around block/MTU boundaries. It records actual
admission, upperbound, wire and roundtrip/size checks. Tighter rejection must be
explicitly reported, never hidden as byte equivalence. No gossip tasks or sockets.

Every fixture/compiler gets a disjoint target root derived from its complete
source/lock/probe identities. Bind the actual Cargo compiler-artifact executable
and SHA, then its complete nonempty native test list before selecting tests.
Require exact selected/pass/filtered counts and matching postflight. Keep the
original owned 1200-second review envelope, 4 GiB floor and five-second capacity/
retirement contracts; compilation/MSRV and original 780/4800/live windows stay
separate. No retry-to-pass, reduced corpus, lint allowance or policy exception.

The M input restored a true bound but tightened nine supported admissions, even
though their original frames fit MTU. Retain that regression. A separate R input
after Z may preserve old admission with a true bound: only for more than two
pending blocks, preview the owned writer and take max(old estimate, preview
length). The observer/contract source and original wide gate stay unchanged.
Require R's actual admission/wire results to match B on all 239 supported cases.
The additional allocation/copy/compression needs later attribution and prevents
automatic product adoption; functional equivalence is not a performance result.

The first preview variant panicked for structurally oversized operations before
the caller could reject them. Retain its failing regression. R2 skips that
preview for items outside append's u16 domain and restores non-mutating rejection.
Its exact extended catalog retains all 105 original tests plus one named test
containing three oversized cases; unknown or missing additions refuse.

The separate S input changes only the LRU requirement/locked node to patched
0.18.2 after the standalone package's unchanged policy exposed 2026-0253.
Product dependency policy remains untouched. Portable source patches are local
review material, not a published crate or a production enrollment receipt.
